using GameManager
using PManager

~ bookshelf
There are many books in the shelf. 
Most of them are about Cloudvale Town. 
Casimir likes reading history and cultures a lot. 
=> END

~ sirens
do show("Casimir", "c_default", "CharacterA")
Casimir: There's a book here about us——the Sirens.
Casimir: Sirens like me are noticeable. You can tell if there are any symbols in our bodies. It's like a birthmark.
Casimir: When Sirens pass away, they become pearls. The quality of the pearl depends on the siren.
Casimir: The brighter it is, the happier their life must've been, and the bigger it is, the more memories they have.
do set_true("about_sirens")
do hide_all()
=> END

~ dragonborns
Casimir: Mostly scary...
Casimir: They're the rarest of all the races. They have horns and sharp eyes.
Casimir: There's barely any of them in Cloudvale ever since the incident...
do set_true("about_dragonborns")
=> END

~ elementals
Casimir: Ah, the Elementals. They're born from many things. Some say if an emotion is so strong, the object gains a physical body.
Casimir: My childhood friend, Hein is an elemental. He was born from the windy forests of Sherbet Mountain.
Casimir: Sirens are usually born from music, though.
Casimir: My mother told me I was born from the music of the sea. I didn't really understand that.
do set_true("about_elementals")
=> END

~ tourists
if is_true("about_tourists"):
	Casimir: Just some books about strangers outside of this world.
	=> END!
if is_true("about_sirens") and is_true("about_elementals") and is_true("about_dragonborns"):
	Casimir: Its a book about... ???
	Casimir: We don't know what to call them, we just call them [b]tourists[/b]
	Casimir: They're beings that come from above the sky and decided to reside here.
	Casimir: But despite the name, we're not really advised to trust them.
	do set_true("about_tourists")
=> END

